# AGENTS.md — `src/{{ package_name }}/` (library layer)

This is the pure, installable, tested library. Code here outlives the paper. Root
`../AGENTS.md` still applies; these are the additional rules for library code.

## Rules
- **No I/O, no analysis orchestration here.** Reading files, writing figures, and
  wiring stages belong in `workflow/`. This layer is functions on data in memory.
- **Pure and small.** Functions ≤ 15 LOC (excluding docstrings). Prefer many small
  composable functions over one large one.
- **Typed.** `mypy --strict` must pass; every public function has type hints and a
  numpydoc docstring (`interrogate` enforces coverage).
- **Vectorize.** Delegate to idiomatic numpy/pandas/scipy; avoid hand-rolled loops
  over arrays. Reach for numba only when profiling justifies it.
- **`pathlib.Path` only** for paths (when a function must take one) — never `os.path`.
- **Determinism.** Any stochastic function takes an explicit seed/`Generator`
  argument; never reads a global RNG.

## Workflow (TDD, non-negotiable)
Red → green → refactor. Write the failing test first.
```bash
pytest tests/ -q                 # unit tests
pytest --hypothesis-show-statistics   # property-based tests on numeric kernels
```
Coverage target: **≥ 90%** for pure functions. Critical math kernels get
`hypothesis` property tests and are candidates for `mutmut` mutation testing.

## Before you finish
- New public function → test + docstring + type hints, or it's not done.
- `pre-commit run --all-files` is green.
